# Negative control of the round-9 additions to the spec (BL015.21 / BL015.23 / PR #44, round 9).
# Two behaviours of `native.Window.settle_commit` that the code already had and the docs already described, and that no test pinned:
#   T1(b) the lateness of the acknowledgement is judged on the read that FIRST saw it, not on the time of the current read: a matching
#         acknowledgement seen in time stays in time whatever the later reads cost. Mutation Sd-b (one expression) survived the 18 tests of
#         the classes `LateAcknowledgement` and `Release`. New test: LateAcknowledgement.test_an_acknowledgement_seen_with_the_picture_is_in_time_even_when_the_slow_reads_that_follow_pass_the_ack_budget
#   T1(c) an acknowledgement that STOPS matching starts over: only its NEXT match counts (a stale first sighting would turn a late match into a
#         dedupe, a false pass). Mutation Sd-c (one line) survived the same 18 tests. New test: LateAcknowledgement.test_an_acknowledgement_that_matched_then_stopped_and_matched_again_after_the_budget_is_unconfirmed_not_deduped
# Plus one EQUIVALENT mutant, Sd-d (the reset of `acked_at` together with `first_at` in the not-converged branch): no read sequence can tell it from
# the real code, so there is no test for it (see the differential below).
# The runners are NOT changed in this round: the only change under test is the spec (scripts/gizmo-perf/gizmo-perf.spec.py, +2 tests, a scripted
# monitor `ScriptedReads` and a round-9 comment); the spec of this round has 254 tests: the 252 of 920d3bb plus 2 ids that it does not have
# (LateAcknowledgement.test_an_acknowledgement_seen_with_the_picture_is_in_time_even_when_the_slow_reads_that_follow_pass_the_ack_budget, LateAcknowledgement.test_an_acknowledgement_that_matched_then_stopped_and_matched_again_after_the_budget_is_unconfirmed_not_deduped), 0 earlier id(s) removed.
