# What each test protects (the direction of each wrong version, from the differential below): Sd-b only ever turns a dedupe into `unconfirmed` (a FALSE
# FAILURE under slow reads, never a false pass); Sd-c only ever turns an `unconfirmed` into a dedupe (a FALSE PASS). A late FIRST sighting of the
# acknowledgement (a slow read that sees it after the budget) is the job of the round 8 test, which both wrong versions keep passing.
